// # Make every product .oo file readable
//
// File: openOODA/DINNER.oot
//
// Logline: Rewrite product .oo files so they read like the scripts: title, logline, beats, then clean code.
//
// Setup: Scripts already have this look. This plan is the same pass on oodac and ooda/std. The owner stays in the loop.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Write this plan in plain words.
//   2. Rewrite a few small files. Run a check. Stop if it fails.
//   3. Wave the rest of ooda/std, then oodac, one file at a time.
//   4. Long files last. Split only if a file does two jobs.
//   5. Owner reads a sample before we call it done.

// ## What this is

Make every product `.oo` file easy to read. Same look as the scripts.
A person opens the file and knows the job before the body.

// ## What a file looks like

  // # <Title>
  //
  // Logline: <one sentence, present tense, ends in a period>.
  //
  // Setup: <what must be true>.
  //
  // Beats:
  //   1. <first beat>
  //   2. <second beat>
  //   3. <third beat>

Title is the job, not the file name.
Logline is one honest sentence.
Beats name what the file does, not line numbers.
Three beats minimum. Six maximum.
If something is not built yet, one `// residual:` line after the header.

Compiler and std files keep real functions. Do not put `when` / `then` in them.
Scripts already use that story in `main`. Leave scripts alone.

Keep function names (`typecheck_*`, `c_emit_*`, `lex_*`, `opt_*`, `res_*`).
Keep behavior. Pretty is not a new API.

// ## Scope

Do:
  ooda/std/*.oo (and small std subfolders)
  ooda/oodac/*.oo

Skip:
  ooda/scripts/*.oo          already done
  ooda/fixtures/**           inputs, not programs
  ooda/bootstrap/corpus/**   inputs
  ooda/pm/**                 other owner
  org /std/src               not this wave unless the owner says so

About 220 files. Not 1500.

// ## How we work

One writer per file. A second agent reads the body, not just the header.
After each small wave, run `oodac check` on the touched files.
If the check fails, fix those files. Do not start the next file.
Writer does not mark their own file done.

Waves of four files.
Small files first.
Files near 256 lines last. Comments count. Split only at a real seam.

Do not rewrite RULES, SCRIPTING, BOOTSTRAP, or SPRINT for this pass.
Do not add Tokenomics stickers.
Caps stay in the function signature.

// ## Check

From ooda/:
  ./oodac/oodac check <file.oo>

Green: next four files.
Red: fix, then re-check.

// ## Done when

Every in-scope file has the academy header and reads top to bottom.
Checks on the rewritten files are green.
The owner looked at a sample and said it looks right.
